  "content": "<p><i>The discovery of a new trench at the bottom of Loch Ness in Scotland has opened up speculation that it could be the home of its legendary monster.</i></p>\n              \n\n              \n                <figure>\n                  <img src=\"https://turntable.kagiso.io/images/loch_ness.2e16d0ba.fill-800x600.jpg\" alt=\"Loch Ness Monster\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" width=\"588\" height=\"441\" />\n                  \n                </figure>\n              \n\n              \n              \n\n              \n\n            \n              \n\n                \n                  <p>According to reports, a sightseeing boat captain, Keith Stewart, discovered an unknown trench 30 metres deeper than the loch's official depth.</p><p>The official depth of Loch Ness is 230 metres, although some reports say depths of 247 metres have been recorded. Stewart's ship recorded a depth of 270 metres.</p><p>Stewart reportedly also claimed to have had a possible Loch Ness Monster sighting on sonar.</p><p>\"I wasn't really a believer of the monster beforehand,\" Stewart told the Scotsman, \"But two weeks ago, I got a sonar image of what looked like a long object with a hump lying at the bottom. It wasn't there when I scanned the loch bed later.\"</p>\n                \n\n                \n\n              \n\n                \n                  \n                \n\n                \n\n              \n\n                \n                  \n                \n\n                \n\n              \n\n                \n                  <p>It must be taken into account that Stewart reportedly operates a ship that brings tourists out to \"discover\" the monster, so the claim has to be met with a certain amount of scepticism.</p><p>Here are some recent sightings of Nessie, as posted on the Official Loch Ness Monster Sightings Register:</p>\n                \n\n                \n\n              \n\n                \n                  \n\n\n<figure>\n  \n      <img src=\"https://turntable.kagiso.io/images/ln1.original.jpg\" alt=\"Loch Ness 1\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" width=\"554\" height=\"253\" />\n      \n        <figcaption>\n          The Official Loch Ness Monster Sightings Register\n        </figcaption>\n      \n    \n</figure>\n\n                \n\n                \n\n              \n\n                \n                  \n\n\n<figure>\n  \n      <img src=\"https://turntable.kagiso.io/images/ln2.original.jpg\" alt=\"Loch Ness 2\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" width=\"555\" height=\"379\" />\n      \n        <figcaption>\n          The Official Loch Ness Monster Sightings Register\n        </figcaption>\n      \n    \n</figure>\n\n                \n\n                \n\n              \n\n                \n                  \n\n\n<figure>\n  \n      <img src=\"https://turntable.kagiso.io/images/ln3.original.jpg\" alt=\"Loch Ness 3\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" width=\"558\" height=\"870\" />\n      \n        <figcaption>\n          The Official Loch Ness Monster Sightings Register\n        </figcaption>\n      \n    \n</figure>\n\n                \n\n                \n\n              \n\n                \n                  \n\n\n<figure>\n  \n      <img src=\"https://turntable.kagiso.io/images/ln4.original.jpg\" alt=\"Loch Ness 4\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" width=\"505\" height=\"855\" />\n      \n        <figcaption>\n          The Official Loch Ness Monster Sightings Register\n        </figcaption>\n      \n    \n</figure>\n\n                \n\n                \n\n              \n\n                \n                  \n\n\n<figure>\n  \n      <img src=\"https://turntable.kagiso.io/images/ln5.original.jpg\" alt=\"Loch Ness 5\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" width=\"558\" height=\"801\" />\n      \n        <figcaption>\n          The Official Loch Ness Monster Sightings Register\n        </figcaption>\n      \n    \n</figure>\n\n                \n\n                \n\n              \n\n                \n                  \n\n\n<figure>\n  \n      <img src=\"https://turntable.kagiso.io/images/ln6.original.jpg\" alt=\"Loch Ness 6\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" width=\"557\" height=\"407\" />\n      \n        <figcaption>\n          The Official Loch Ness Monster Sightings Register\n        </figcaption>\n      \n    \n</figure>"
